# font-demo

A portrait of the committed font tables, held long enough to be read. It draws
two lines at sixteen pixels and two at twelve, centred on the panel, the last
one in the Polish charset, so a person can tell a working font from a
scrambled one. Below them it lays out every glyph of the twelve pixel table,
wrapped to the panel's width, so no bitmap in the charset goes unseen.

It branches on the panel's depth: a one-bit panel receives the composed packed
rows directly, and a sixteen-bit panel receives each row expanded to RGB565
black on white. Either way the composition is the same one-bit frame, which is
the point of mm.fonts: the text knows nothing about the panel.

It names mm.fonts for the tables and the composition, mm.display for the
frame, and mm.mcu for the hold, and no board, SDK, or vendor.
